Author: Nick <nick.eventslight@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 10:51:51 2026 +0100

    usb2: PHY-B enumerates at High Speed -- IDELAY tap 8 + OE from post-delay dir
    
    USB2 on the custom SODIMM breakout is alive:
    
        usb 1-10: new high-speed USB device number 18 using xhci_hcd
        usb 1-10: New USB device found, idVendor=1209, idProduct=eab2
        usb 1-10: Product: N-Series AVB Switchover Backup
        card 3 [Backup]: USB-Audio at usb-0000:00:14.0-10, high speed
    
    Recipe:
        BOARD=breakout USB_BACKUP=1 USB_PHASE=0 USB_IDELAY_TAP=8 \
          BUILD_DIR=build_probe_bk2 ../.venv/bin/python3 build_probe.py
    
    Two independent faults, both required:
    
    1. DIR/NXT transposed in the hand-wiring (USB_SWAP_DIRNXT=1, committed earlier
       as the platform default).
    2. USB_IDELAY_TAP=8. yosys+nextpnr-xilinx inserts no IOB input flop and no
       automatic IDELAY, so the IOB->first-flop ROUTING delay sets the ULPI
       sampling point -- and it changes every rebuild as placement shuffles. Two
       unconstrained P&R runs of the identical design gave `error -71` and no D+
       pull-up at all. avb-aes3 solved this with a firmware-tunable tap
       (ulpi_idelay_tap, CSR reset 8); this project needed the same number.
    
    usb_utmi_top.py: drive the data-bus OE from dir_s (post-IDELAY) instead of the
    raw ulpi.dir.i. THIS IS WHAT MADE IDELAY ROUTABLE. Every prior attempt parked
    at exactly overused=3 forever -- VAR_LOAD, VARIABLE with a shared CE, FIXED,
    FIXED with i_C tied off, and FIXED with a BUFG on REFCLK plus injected
    create_clock. Asking one pad for both a delayed and an undelayed copy of itself
    is unroutable by construction: a 7-series input path is
    PAD -> IBUF -> (IDELAY | direct), a one-of-two mux, not a fan-out. Router then
    went overused=1 -> 0 at iteration 7. A constant overuse count that is immune to
    every knob is a structural impossibility, not congestion. With no IDELAY,
    dir_s IS ulpi.dir.i, so PHY-A cannot regress.
    
    usb_utmi_top.py: USB_PROBE=1 adds a UTMI-level enumeration probe, env-gated
    inside the real design rather than a copy so it cannot drift from the known-good
    config. Prints over the R3 UART at 115200:
    
        SF=FFFF SU=0014 DA=0023 AK=0016 RE=0000 TV=003C LS=0 S=80 06 00 01 00 00 40 00
    
    SF counts SOFs, which the host emits every 125 us forever -- a free always-on RX
    monitor. AK counts ACKs FROM the host, which clears our TX outright. S= is the
    first SETUP payload, and because the host's first request is always
    GET_DESCRIPTOR(device) = 80 06 00 01 00 00 40 00, the expected value is a
    built-in control: anything else is RX corruption caught red-handed.
    
    usb_descriptors.py + usb_utmi_top.py: per-PHY identity, following USB_BACKUP so
    a build cannot be mislabelled. Main = eab1/serial 0, Backup = eab2/serial 1.
    product_id was hardcoded; it is now plumbed to d.idProduct. The separate-PID
    split follows upstream adat-usb2-audio-interface. NOTE 0x1209/0xEAB2 is a
    pid.codes slot that must actually be allocated to this project -- USB_PID=0xeab1
    puts both ports back on one PID.
    
    build_probe.py: injects the create_clock / set_clock_groups lines the Amaranth
    Xray template omits, as build_dac.py already did. Without them nextpnr times
    every path blind (usb_clk reported "PASS at 12.00 MHz"); with them it reports
    PASS at the real 60.00 MHz. That matters more here than for timing reports,
    since placement quality IS the sampling point.
    
    bitstreams/archive.sh: `|| true` on the builder-detection grep. Under
    set -euo pipefail a grep that matched nothing killed the script AFTER copying
    the .bit but BEFORE writing the .info -- the mechanism behind this tree's "44 of
    52 bitstreams have no recipe". It fired for every builder taking BUILD_DIR from
    the environment. Adds an ARCHIVE_BUILDER= override for those.
    
    platform.py: withdraw the unsupported claim that IOB=TRUE or IOI clock
    resources were behind the IDELAY routing failure, and record what it actually
    was.
    
    Tap 8 is verified on three different placements but NOT bracketed -- build taps
    4 and 12 to learn the real margin.
    
